{
 "schema": 1,
 "provenance": {
  "tool": "tune_table.py of the split kernels' tuning tools (kernel source snapshot 3b377cd), reduced as their merge_table.py does",
  "measurement": "the kernels' standalone runner: whole launch graph, p50 of 100 rounds after 20 warm-up rounds, cold L2; each GPU pinned to the RDMA NIC on its PCIe switch. Anchors 16, 32, 64, 128 and 256 (2026-11-25): balanced routes, packed cross-NUMA dispatch off (MEGAMOE_XNUMA_PACK=0), as the adapter of FlashInfer 0dc6f0785abd ran it. Anchor 96 (2026-11-26): balanced and power_law routes (Zipf exponent 1.0), packed dispatch on as the runner selects it",
  "setup": "EP16 over two hosts of 8 GPUs each (two NUMA nodes of 4 GPUs per host), 156 SMs per GPU",
  "fields": "p50_us: the selected configuration on balanced routes; default_us: the rule-based configuration, same runner; power_law_us / default_power_law_us: the same pair on power_law routes; confirm: the pairs on a second route seed",
  "selection": "anchors 16 to 256: the tuner's selection per anchor on balanced routes, except 32 rows (see its note); with the packed dispatch the same tuner selects the same knobs at 16, 64, 128 and 256 rows, and at 128 rows the two-route rule below ends on the same knobs. Anchor 96: the two-route rule (tune_two_routes.py --rule sequential: the rule-based default is the first baseline; a candidate more than 0.5% slower than the current baseline on balanced or on power_law routes is excluded, otherwise it replaces the baseline if the mean of its two times is lower; a power_law time is the median of 3 trials). Every anchor was then timed through this backend's wrapper with a reference check of the output",
  "untuned": "anchors that name only the transport keep FlashInfer's rule-based selection for the row buckets above the tuned decode sizes",
  "ep8_placements": "the three ep8_2numa tables are FlashInfer's own table for 384 expert slots at EP8 on 156 SMs, registered unchanged for 408, 416 and 448 slots (a static placement with 3, 4 or 8 replica slots per rank at EP8): FlashInfer selects a table by the exact slot count, so without them such a placement runs the rule-based selection. The knobs are not tuned at these slot counts. The solver of the placement decides the slot count (it copies only experts above its load threshold), so check the count of the file you serve"
 },
